Determine the type of Defense Evasion Techniques Leveraging Exploitation and External Influence
Your answer: Deploy Container

After the attacker infiltrated the target system, they discovered Docker was installed. Subsequently, the attacker downloaded and ran a malicious image named 'malicious-docker' on the system. One of the reasons for executing the malicious image within Docker is to reduce the likelihood of detection and minimize visibility. This technique can be associated with 'Deploy Container' (T1610) in defense evasion.

